{"title":"List of Holy Roman Empresses","text":"List of Holy Roman Empresses
Holy Roman Empress or Empress of the Holy Roman Empire is the title given to the consort (wife) or regent of the Holy Roman Emperor.

 The elective dignity of Holy Roman Emperor was restricted to males only, therefore there was never a Holy Roman Empress regnant, though women such as Theophanu or Maria Theresa of Austria, who controlled the power of rule, served as de facto Empresses regnant.","entities":["Holy Roman Empress","Holy Roman Emperor","Theophanu","Maria Theresa of Austria","Holy Roman Empire"],"facts":["Free Imperial City of Frankfurt -LOCATED_IN-> Holy Roman Empire","Electorate of Bavaria -LOCATED_IN-> Holy Roman Empire"]}

{"title":"Eat to Live","text":"Eat to Live
Eat to Live: The Amazing Nutrient-Rich Program for Fast and Sustained Weight Loss is a book written in 2003 by Dr. Joel Fuhrman, which he revised in 2011.

 The book offers a formula: health = nutrients / calories.","entities":[],"facts":[]}

{"title":"Scarsdale diet","text":"Scarsdale diet
The Scarsdale diet is a fad diet designed for weight loss created in the 1970s by Herman Tarnower, named for the town in New York where he practiced cardiology, described in the book "The Complete Scarsdale Medical Diet plus Dr. Tarnower's Lifetime Keep-Slim Program", which Tarnower wrote with an author of self-help books, Sam Sinclair Baker.

 The diet carries potential health risks and does not instill the kind of healthy eating habits required for sustainable weight loss.","entities":[],"facts":[]}

{"title":"Diet food","text":"Diet food
Diet food (or dietetic food) refers to any food or beverage whose recipe is altered to reduce fat, carbohydrates, and/or sugar in order to make it part of a weight loss program or diet.

 Such foods are usually intended to assist in weight loss or a change in body type, although bodybuilding supplements are designed to aid in gaining weight or muscle.","entities":["weight","Diet food","weight loss program","diet","bodybuilding supplements","muscle","body type"],"facts":["weight -PART_OF-> person","Diet food -PART_OF-> weight loss program","Diet food -PART_OF-> diet"]}

